# GraphQL resolver errors

A GraphQL resolver must not return a plain `error`. gqlgen publishes
`fmt.Errorf`, `errors.New`, and `graphql.ErrorOnPath` with no
`extensions.code`. The tracing logger then records the operation as
`UNKNOWN` at error level.

Return a helper from `pkg/server/gqlx`. Do not build `&gqlerror.Error` by
hand. A hand-built error can set `extensions.code`, but it skips the
helpers that set the path and the message.

`r.authorize` already returns a coded error. Return that error unchanged.

## Which code

- The row the field was supposed to load is missing: `gqlx.NotFound`, or
  `gqlx.MapError` when the same call can also fail for another reason.
  `MapError` maps `coredata.ErrResourceNotFound` to `NOT_FOUND` and
  `validator.ValidationErrors` to `INVALID`. Anything else is logged and
  returned as `INTERNAL`.
- The load failed and not-found is already handled: log with
  `r.logger.ErrorCtx` and return `gqlx.Internal(ctx)`. Do not put
  `err.Error()` in the response.
- The client sent a value the server refuses: `gqlx.Invalid` /
  `Invalidf`, `Unauthenticated` / `Unauthenticatedf`, `Forbidden` /
  `Forbiddenf`, `Conflict`, or another named helper in
  `pkg/server/gqlx/errors.go`.
- The schema already models absence as null (no alias, no generated
  document): return `nil, nil`. That is not an error.

A new resolver-owned code needs a helper in `pkg/server/gqlx/errors.go`
and an entry in `safeGraphQLErrorCodes` in `pkg/server/gqlx/tracing.go`.
A gqlgen protocol code such as `GRAPHQL_PARSE_FAILED` or
`COMPLEXITY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` is not returned by a resolver; it only needs
the allowlist entry. A code missing from that list is logged as `UNKNOWN`
at error level. `INTERNAL` stays at error. Every other allowlisted code
logs at info.

```go
// GOOD — missing row or store failure. MapError sends err.Error() for
// NOT_FOUND. Wrap the sentinel only with client-safe text, or return
// NotFoundf(ctx, "resource not found") when the prefix must stay private.
doc, err := r.probo.Documents.Get(ctx, scope, documentID)
if err != nil {
	return nil, gqlx.MapError(ctx, r.logger, "cannot get document", err)
}

// GOOD — not-found already returned; the rest is internal.
// NotFound shows err.Error() too; use NotFoundf when that text is not client-safe.
owner, err := loaders.Profile.Load(ctx, ownerID)
if errors.Is(err, coredata.ErrResourceNotFound) {
	return nil, gqlx.NotFound(ctx, err)
}
if err != nil {
	r.logger.ErrorCtx(ctx, "cannot get owner", log.Error(err))
	return nil, gqlx.Internal(ctx)
}

// BAD — no code; logged as UNKNOWN and the store error reaches the client
if err != nil {
	return nil, fmt.Errorf("cannot get document: %w", err)
}
```

This does not apply to MCP resolvers. See
[`contrib/claude/graphql.md`](../../contrib/claude/graphql.md) and
[`contrib/claude/api-surface.md`](../../contrib/claude/api-surface.md).
